@startuml credentials-lifecycle
title Credential Lifecycle: Independent Validity and Retention

|Credential issuance|
start
:CredentialRegistryFactory_Issue;
:Anchorers and holders authorize initial creation;
:Create one canonical registered credential;
stop

|Intrinsic credential renewal|
start
:Credential implementing CredentialLifecycle
with an existing validUntil;
if (Registered demo template?) then (yes)
  :Reject anchorer-only CredentialLifecycle_Renew;
  :Use RegisteredCredentialLifecycle_Renew
with explicit registry authorization;
else (unregistered)
  :CredentialLifecycle_Renew by anchorers;
endif
:Require later validUntil; preserve other credential fields;
:On registered renewal preserve all registration fields,
including possibly absent expiresAt;
:Time alone determines natural intrinsic expiry;
:No automatic ledger archival;
stop

|Registration extension candidate|
start
:RegisteredCredentialLifecycle_ExtendRegistration;
:Require later existing expiresAt;
:Candidate controllers are anchorers and registry admin;
:Replacement retains anchorer-and-holder signatories;
:Replace canonical contract with identical credential view;
:Preserve registeredAt, registryAdmin, and meta;
:Only registry expiresAt advances;
:validUntil may differ or be absent;
:DSO payment adapter not implemented;
stop

|Holder operations|
start
:Canonical Credential with 0..n holders and 1..n anchorers;
if (One holder relinquishes?) then (yes)
  :Credential_RemoveSelfAsHolder;
  :Consume old contract and create one replacement;
  :Remove only the exercising holder, including the final holder;
  :Preserve anchorers, remaining holder order,
credential validity, and registration data;
else (all holders archive)
  :Credential_ArchiveAsAllHolders;
  :All current holders authorize, or anchorers if holderless;
  :Credential_ArchiveAsAnchorers is also available independently;
  :Consume the canonical contract as a terminal operation;
endif
stop

note right
The separate lifecycle operations are:
CredentialRegistryFactory_Issue, CredentialLifecycle_Renew,
RegisteredCredentialLifecycle_Renew, and
RegisteredCredentialLifecycle_ExtendRegistration.

RegisteredCredential is registration-only and requires Credential.
RegisteredCredentialLifecycle requires RegisteredCredential,
CredentialLifecycle, and compiler-required transitive Credential.
The registered demo implements all four interfaces.

Dates are independent, including when either is absent.
The registered choices use candidate replacement authority;
DSO governance and paid extension protocol remain unresolved.
end note

@enduml
